{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And it is healed.</b> One must investigate what this word comes to teach. However, in Torat Kohanim it expounds: ״פרח״ — can this be a שחין? etc. Scripture says ונרפא. The meaning is: if one was struck by something that brings about a שחין, for example he was struck by wood or by stone, and the flesh swelled at the site of the blow, and afterward a שחין spread in it — it should not be impure unless it healed, i.e., the flesh returned at the site of the blow and the שחין spread in it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:07.253206517Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}